{
  "about": [
    "Shared test vectors of the JKNet relay protocol, version 1: the relay node of JKNet Online and the host tunnel of the JKNet launcher check themselves against this file.",
    "Byte strings are lowercase hex unless the key says base64 or base64url. Integers are JSON numbers; every one here is below 2^53. A session id is 16 lowercase hex characters, the big-endian u64 of the wire, as the API writes it.",
    "nodeSecret is the 32-byte node secret. keyId is its generation: the first byte of HMAC-SHA256(secret, ASCII 'JKNet relay key id v1').",
    "account.userRef is the first 16 bytes of SHA-256 of the account id as UTF-8.",
    "hostKey.input is the ASCII label, the 8-byte session id and the 16-byte user ref, concatenated; hostKey.hex is the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA256(node secret, input).",
    "ticket.hex is the whole ticket: the signed part (ticket.signedPart) followed by the 16-byte MAC, the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA256(node secret, signed part). The API hands it to the launcher as ticket.base64url, unpadded.",
    "messages[].hex is a whole UDP datagram: the 14-byte header (magic 4a4b52, version 01, type, flags 00, session id), the body and, when signed is true, the first 8 bytes of HMAC-SHA256(hostKey.hex, everything before them). PING and PONG carry session id 0 and no signature; a PING is padded with zeros to 64 bytes.",
    "messages[].fields names the body fields of the protocol table in camelCase. ticket, payload and nodeId are hex; publicIpv4 is dotted.",
    "Fixed-size bodies have exactly their listed length: a receiver drops a message with extra bytes. rejected[] lists datagrams a receiver must drop, with the reason."
  ],
